              "type": "Text",
              "value": {
                "string": "e À gt ; Eq 10 in which C I is constant. In the case of complete deactivation, as t!1, I ! I OFF ¼ b I g , where I OFF represents the LuxI concentration in the OFF state. On the other hand, at t = 0, I ON t¼0 ¼ b I g þ C I ¼ I OFF þ C I . Therefore, since cells are initially in the ON state at t = 0, C I can be calculated as C I = I ON -I OFF , where I ON t¼0 denotes the LuxI concentration in initially ON cells and I ON denotes the LuxI concentration in the ON steady state. By substituting the value of C I in Eq 10, we can obtain the value of I(t) in initially ON cells as follows: I ON t¼0 ðtÞ ¼ I OFF þ ðI ON À I OFF Þe À gt ; Eq 11 where I ON t¼0 ðtÞ denotes the LuxI concentration at time t past dilution initially ON cells. The ratio of the LuxI concentration in the ON state, denoted as I ON , to the LuxI concentration in the OFF state, denoted as I OFF , is defined as the Fold Change (FC), and can be expressed as I ON I OFF . Fold change in expression of a target gene expressed under QS regulation is a measure of the promoter activity in active to inactive states. Using this definition, Eq 11 can be rewritten as:"
              }
